1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,700
Guilin or Zhangjiajie for your first China trip? I'm your China Travel Expert.

2
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:05,100
Everyone tells you to go to the Avatar mountains.

3
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:07,600
Zhangjiajie: 3,000 sandstone pillars, a 239 yuan four-day pass.

4
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:10,000
But you'll hike, queue, and ride a 65 yuan cliff elevator.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,500
Guilin is one slow boat down the Li River.

6
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:15,100
215 yuan, 60 kilometers, the peaks off the 20 yuan note.

7
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:17,600
Double-tap if you'd pick the boat.

8
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:20,200
My verdict: first trip, Guilin wins. Less climbing, more postcard.

9
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:22,800
Zhangjiajie is the better trip. Save it for your second.

10
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:25,600
★ Expert Tip: book both parks online, real-name, bring your passport.

11
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:28,200
So, first-timer: boat or pillars? Tell me I'm wrong.
